1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,216
Want to buy a migraine? Just five dollars, perfectly fresh and ready for your nervous system.

2
00:00:06,516 --> 00:00:15,684
I extract my own physical agony and bottle it, selling every sharp stab to people who prefer my pain to theirs.

3
00:00:15,984 --> 00:00:24,384
Business is booming because everyone wants an easy life, leaving me broke, broken, but completely pain-free.

4
00:00:24,684 --> 00:00:31,668
Then an old man walks in, placing a heavy, pitch-black jar onto my dusty glass counter.

5
00:00:31,968 --> 00:00:40,656
He whispers that it holds the ultimate agony, a localized heart-stopping torture worth a thousand normal lifetimes.

6
00:00:40,956 --> 00:00:48,756
Curiosity wins. I pay him my entire life savings just to taste what true suffering feels like.

7
00:00:49,056 --> 00:00:57,096
I open the lid, and the invisible terror rushes straight into my chest, shattering every breath.

8
00:00:57,396 --> 00:01:04,692
As my vision fades, I look in the dusty mirror and finally recognize the old man's face.

9
00:01:04,992 --> 00:01:12,312
It was me. Older, scarred, sending my worst nightmare back through time just to survive another day.

10
00:01:12,612 --> 00:01:18,828
Want to buy a migraine? Just five dollars, perfectly fresh and ready for your nervous system.
